entine asked  Jensen how big is this Market the market  is gigantic and growing in size every  day as some of the world's biggest and  most ambitious companies invest in deep  learning techniques to fight disease  build the next generation of autonomous  vehicles and revolutionize the Natural  Sciences there's a very good chance  they're doing so with Nvidia use there  was no looking back in April 2020 Nvidia  spent seven billion dollars to acquire  melanox a Next Generation networking  company since then it's tripled the  revenue generated by his data center  stream that's allowed Nvidia to pull off  the sort of Revenue growth that usually  only hot startups can enjoy in 2020  Nvidia announced it had generated about  11 billion dollars in Revenue over the  previous fiscal year last year that  figure jumped to 16.6 billion and in  February of 2020 Nvidia announced it had  generated an insane 26.9 billion dollars  in Revenue that's 60 increase from the  previous year for a 30 year old company  remember the business model an open  development ecosystem that can be  deployed only on Nvidia Hardware Cuda  and Nvidia gpus dominate several  application areas including deep  learning and underpin some of the  fastest computers in the world Nvidia  generates 8 billion dollars of free cash  flow every year and has more than 20  billion on hand whereas at the turn of  the 90s they had a 30 gross margin today  their margin sits at 66 percent they  have built and fortified one of the  world's deepest moats I want to talk  briefly about power and how companies  can wield it one common form of power is  the ability to choose where you operate  on the price curve that kind of power is  usually reserved for monopolies another  form of power is the ability to make  your competitors react to you rather  than the other way around that kind of  power is reserved for companies that  create new technologies in New Markets  it's very rare to wield both forms of  power let alone at the same time but  that's just what Nvidia was able to  accomplish by pioneering the emulation  of Graphics chips it could deliver cost  customers what they cared about most  sheer performance by creating truly  programmable gpus it leveraged parallel  architectures to massively accelerate  performance and just as the revenue from  that established technology was  beginning to Plateau it found a new use  case for its technology in the form of  enabling huge advances in machine  learning all while locking in consumers  and Enterprise customers into a  proprietary ecosystem that's real power  no one can predict the future but as  long as Jensen is in the driver's seat  Nvidia will never stop innovating  they're making a play for automotive  meaning the electric vehicle and  autonomous vehicle software stack Jensen  thinks that's a 300 billion addressable  market and another project with massive  potential is nvidia's Omniverse the  Omniverse isn't like the metaverse it's  not a place where you can walk around  commute to work or speculate on digital  property it's useful here to look at  Earth too the supercomputer project  Nvidia announced in late 2021. Earth 2  will combine GPU accelerated Computing  deep learning and observed and modeled  data to simulate ultra high res  resolution climate models in a world  where one-to-one scale simulations are  possible it's easy to imagine any  company simulating how their new product  or service will work in the Omniverse  before deploying it in the real world it  could be running the world's most  sophisticated climate models on a  replica digital Earth or space startups  simulating atmospheric effects or their  prototype vehicles or new pharmaceutical  firms finding hundreds of new molecules  that could hold the key to curing some  of the world's most persistent and  devastating diseases if the technology  is there then there's no limit the  Omniverse is an extremely ambitious  concept because nothing like it has ever  really existed but in a way it's easier  to see it working out partly that's down  to Jensen's unbelievable track record of  delivering moonshots but it's also  because it's easier to see the  continuity between the Omniverse and the  immense scientific discovery Nvidia has  enabled through Cuda Jensen of course  saw the potential of simulation from a  long way off in 2006 Nvidia invested in  a company that was creating a navigable  software model of the Earth back then it  was called Keyhole but today we know it  is Google Earth simulation holds in  incredible promise for accelerating  scientific discovery by an order of  magnitude one of the biggest reasons why  is that simulation already saved Nvidia  it's what enabled it to defy Moore's Law  and Pioneer chip emulation it was  critical to the development of the first  consumer gpus and it is the principal  underlying Cuda but most of all nvidia's  Extraordinary capacity for simulation  has allowed millions of people to do  what Jensen Wong promised when he  started the company 30 years ago tell  better stories thanks for watching I  hope you enjoyed this video and if you'd  like to go a bit deeper please just  watch this video next
 

